{"id":"2014-RPR","predecessor":["2012-RPR"],"counts":{"same":27,"changed":7},"items":[{"status":"same","key":"table-division-skill-level","old_key":"table-division-skill-level","old_version":"2012-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"table","path":[]},{"status":"changed","key":"top~p1","old_key":"top~p1","old_version":"2012-RPR","sim":0.981,"conf":"high","t":"para","path":[],"diff":[["=","This new structure and points recorded will be effective January 1,"],["-","2012,"],["+","2014,"],["=","and past points will not be affected. The Tiers are based solely on the number of competitors and not the size of the Event. The Competitor's Points Registry is meant as a tool to assist both the Promoter and the Contestant."]]},{"status":"same","key":"top~p2","old_key":"top~p2","old_version":"2012-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"para","path":[]},{"status":"changed","key":"top~p3","old_key":"top~p3","old_version":"2012-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"para","path":[],"diff":[["=","The"],["-","event director"],["+","Event Director"],["=","is responsible to report the results of Jack & Jill competitions to the WSDC within 10 days of their event. They are also responsible for advising the WSDC how many contestants were in each category, thereby setting up the Tier level for recording points, as stated below. Event Directors are also responsible for informing contestants of the point structure detailed below. The WSDC determines recorded points based on this input. Points are not input into the database until full results and dollar surcharge are turned into the WSDC."]]},{"status":"same","key":"top~p4","old_key":"top~p4","old_version":"2012-RPR","sim":1.0,"conf":"high","t":"para","path":[]},{"status":"changed","key":"top~p5","old_key":"top~p5","old_version":"2012-RPR","sim":0.661,"conf":"high","t":"para","path":[],"diff":[["=","Points are recorded as follows: When number of competitors is “uneven”, points will be recorded"],["+","(Tiered)"],["=","separately by leader/follower. The m